# Line endings — LF everywhere, including checkout on Windows (CI on
# windows-latest, Stage 5). Without this, git on Windows by default
# (core.autocrlf=true) turns \n into \r\n, and both `dart format
# --set-exit-if-changed` and byte-for-byte comparisons break for a reason
# that has nothing to do with the code.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Fixtures are compared byte-for-byte — both the sources and expected.md.
# No conversion in either direction: a nasty fixture with CRLF or in
# Windows-1251 (git would consider it text in the absence of NUL bytes)
# must stay exactly as it was put there.
core/test/fixtures/** -text
